# Optional corporate root CA for Docker npm installs (registry.npmjs.org behind SSL inspection).
#
# 1. Export your organization's root CA as PEM (often from IT or browser cert export).
# 2. Save as:  certs/docker-ca.pem   (same folder as this file; do not commit secrets to git)
# 3. Rebuild:  docker compose build --no-cache
#
# If you cannot obtain the CA file, docker-compose.yml sets NPM_STRICT_SSL=false for dev builds
# (disables npm TLS verification inside the image only).
